---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Layout title="Print your own 3D model">
 <section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Custom printing</span></p><p class="eyebrow kicker">Your file, made physical</p><h1>Off the screen.<br/>Into your hands.</h1><p class="lede">Have a model ready to go? Send it over and tell us what you need. We'll review the details and put together a quote.</p></div></section>
 <section class="container section service-grid"><div class="service-content"><h2>Let's print your next idea.</h2><p>Whether it's one piece or a few, we start by looking at your model, the intended use, and the details that matter to you.</p><p>Include as much as you know:</p><ul><li>Your model file: STL, 3MF, or OBJ</li><li>Target dimensions and the units used in your file</li><li>Quantity and preferred color or material</li><li>What the part will be used for</li><li>Any deadline and your delivery preference</li></ul><p>Not sure about material or print settings? Choose “Help me decide” on the request form. We'll work through the options with you.</p><a class="button" href="/project/?type=print">Send your model <Icon name="upload" size={18}/></a></div><aside class="service-aside"><p class="eyebrow kicker">How it works</p><h2>Three steps to a real thing.</h2><div class="process-row"><span>01</span><div><h3>Send the file.</h3><p>Upload your model with the size, quantity, and any notes we should know.</p></div></div><div class="process-row"><span>02</span><div><h3>Review your quote.</h3><p>We'll confirm the approach, pricing, and timing before you commit.</p></div></div><div class="process-row"><span>03</span><div><h3>Collect your print.</h3><p>We'll arrange shipping or let you know when it's ready for Everett pickup.</p></div></div></aside></section>
 <section class="custom-section section"><div class="container faq-list"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Do I need to know the print settings?</summary><p>No. Tell us how you intend to use the part and what matters most—appearance, fit, strength, or something else. We'll review the requirements together.</p></details><details><summary>Can you change a model before printing?</summary><p>Tell us what you'd like to change. We can review the design work alongside the print request and include it in the quote.</p></details><details><summary>What if I only have a sketch?</summary><p>Start with our design request. Reference photos, rough dimensions, and a description are useful starting points.</p><a class="text-link" href="/design-services/">Get design help <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></details><details><summary>How much will my print cost?</summary><p>Pricing depends on the model, size, quantity, material, and any design or finishing work. We review the project and quote it before printing.</p></details></div></section>
</Layout>
